+# Glossary
+
+**Billing period** — the half-open date range `[period_start, period_end)` a subscription has
+paid for; the renewal is billed on `period_end`. During a trial, the current period is the trial.
+
+**Plan change** — a request to move a subscription to another plan and/or interval
+(`BillingService.change_plan`). Its *target* is the plan and interval the customer asks for.
+
+**Upgrade** — a plan change to a plan with a higher monthly list price, whatever the interval.
+Applies immediately and is prorated. See ADR 0001.
+
+**Downgrade** — a plan change to a plan with a lower monthly list price, whatever the interval.
+Never applies mid-period; it becomes a scheduled change.
+
+**Interval switch** — moving between monthly and annual billing. Never applies mid-period
+(outside a trial); it becomes a scheduled change.
+
+**Scheduled change** — the plan and interval a subscription moves to at its next renewal. At
+most one per subscription; a new plan change replaces it; requesting the current plan and
+interval cancels it.
+
+**Proration** — billing an upgrade for only the rest of the current period: a *credit line*
+for the old plan and a *charge line* for the new plan, each
+`price × remaining_days / period_days` in calendar days, rounded half-up to cents per line.
+
+**Remaining days** — days from the change date (inclusive) to the period end (exclusive).
+
+**Period days** — calendar length of the current billing period: 28–31 for a month, 365 or 366
+for a year.
